                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I first learned about this game on online sites (such as girlsgames.com etc.)- I was only a kid back then, and now some 7 years later I have now discovered that this is an actual full game!\r\n\r\nI've never played the previous entries- so my perspective will be just based on the game itself.\r\n\r\nSome cons I've found: for some reason the links to buy the previous games (which are not on steam) do not work for me? I'm not quite sure what would be the cause outside of me using a less commmon search engine (but I've never run into this issue before). Another person in the reviews also mentioned that previously they advertised the game as having an extra 10 levels, which are very much absent. I've found guides mentioning them- not quite sure what happened there. I did not go into the game thinking there would be more- so I won't factor this in as a con but I will mention it here. \r\n\r\nWhen it comes to management sims it's a great game. I found I really like the visuals and the variety. I think it was a very good choice to switch up the locations- it keeps things fresh and exciting. I've been looking for more games exactly like this- 2D and a cross between a cooking sim/management sim. I think a lot of the mechanics blend together very well. The only one I found myself not really utilizing is Paige but that's due to my own personal taste. \r\n\r\nDifficulty wise- I think it can be challenging to get the 3 stars on Normal difficulty but I've never found myself struggling too much. As long as you get a decent menu set up and are good at these games it shouldn't be too hard. A good balance between a challenge yet not frustrating. I'm yet to try the harder mode. \r\n\r\nOverall decently fun- and I got about 9 hours of play to complete everything [which should round out to around $2,67~ (conversion- i did not buy in USD) per hour so pretty decent value]. I think the artstyle is charming and works well. With the difficulty setting, you could also play it for longer. The story is okay - good enough to sustain some intrigue between levels. Pretty fun! \r\n\r\n",
